---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ToolHero from '../components/ToolHero.astro';
import { tool } from '../data/tools';

const vivary = tool('vivary');
---

<Base
  title="Vivary"
  description="Typed memory, search, and human gates for AI-agent workspaces, kept as plain Markdown files you can open and diff. One command scaffolds a workspace."
>
  <ToolHero tool={vivary} />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div>
        <h2 class="section-title">What it does</h2>
        <p>
          Coding agents forget between sessions and overwrite each other within them.
          Vivary gives a project a small, typed memory that agents read at the start of
          work and write back to under rules you set.
        </p>
      </div>
      <dl class="lanes">
        <div class="lane">
          <dt>Files, not a database</dt>
          <dd>
            Every record is Markdown in your repository. You can open it, diff it, and
            revert it with git. A new workspace starts with five small files.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="lane">
          <dt>Typed context</dt>
          <dd>
            Records have a declared type and a bounded size, so an agent gets the evidence
            it needs for a task and not the whole history.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="lane">
          <dt>Receipts and gates</dt>
          <dd>
            Work carries provenance. A change to memory proposes a plan first, and the
            plan applies only after you approve it. A doctor command checks the
            workspace and rolls back a failed write.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="lane">
          <dt>Fits a project you already have</dt>
          <dd>
            An existing repository keeps its own structure and gets at most three Vivary
            files.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Start a workspace</h2>
        <p>One command, Python 3.11 or newer. The npm launcher runs the same scaffolder.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="snippets">
        <pre><code>uvx create-vivary init my-workspace --preset coding
uvx create-vivary doctor my-workspace</code></pre>
        <pre><code>npx @vivary/create my-workspace --preset coding</code></pre>
        <p>
          The <a href={vivary.docs}>docs</a> cover presets, the record command, and
          adopting an existing project.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="section-title">Status</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        In development. The scaffolder is published on <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@vivary/create">npm</a> and <a href="https://pypi.org/project/create-vivary/">PyPI</a> under MIT.
        A desktop app is being built and is not released.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .snippets {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
</style>
